          "level": "fallback",
          "summary": "Add infringement remedies (procure/modify/replace, else refund) and carve M&I's § 14.2(B) indemnity out of the 3-month liability cap with a 3x annual fees super-cap.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] M&I's indemnity is presently capped at three months' payments by § 13.4, well below our fallback super-cap of 3x annual fees, and there is no continuity remedy for an infringement claim. We have added procure/modify/replace with a fee refund if none is available, and set the § 14.2(B) indemnity cap at 3x annual fees; all other wording of § 13.4 is unchanged.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "insert_after",
              "paragraphId": "p0220",
              "numbering": "C.",
              "text": "C. Infringement Remedies. If a claim described in clause (i) of Section 14.2(B) is made, M&I shall procure for Customer the right to continue using the affected Services or software, or modify or replace it so that it is non-infringing. If none of those remedies is available, M&I shall refund to Customer the fees paid for the affected Services or software.",
              "asHeading": false
            },
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0207",
              "oldText": "M&I's total liability under this Agreement shall not exceed payments made to M&I by Customer under this Agreement during the three (3) months prior to the event. No lawsuit or other action may be brought by either party hereto, or on any claim or controversy based upon or arising in any way out of this Agreement be brought, after one (1) year from the date on which the cause of action arose; provided, however, the foregoing limitation shall not apply to the collection of any amounts due under this Agreement.",
              "newText": "M&I's total liability under this Agreement shall not exceed payments made to M&I by Customer under this Agreement during the three (3) months prior to the event, except that M&I's liability for its indemnification obligations under Section 14.2(B) shall not exceed three (3) times the annual fees paid to M&I by Customer under this Agreement. No lawsuit or other action may be brought by either party hereto, or on any claim or controversy based upon or arising in any way out of this Agreement be brought, after one (1) year from the date on which the cause of action arose; provided, however, the foregoing limitation shall not apply to the collection of any amounts due under this Agreement."
